  data: {
    LLM: "Count the Jacks! Since there are 8 Jacks in the double deck (48 or 64 variants), knowing how many have fallen is critical for controlling the endgame.\n\nThe 'Hidden Trump' Bluff: Use your weak suits early to force the bidder to reveal trumps. If they reveal a suit they aren't strong in, you can take control of the board.\n\nCard Distillation: In a double deck, 'dups' (duplicate cards) are common. Professional players track not just the suit, but which specific duplicate has been played to predict the remaining hand structures.",
